    "content": "Trump Accounts are tax-advantaged investment accounts for U.S. citizen children under 18, established by the 2025 \"One Big Beautiful Bill Act.\" Launching July 4, 2026, they provide a $1,000 government-seeded, parent-managed investment vehicle for children born between 2025–2028, with up to $5,000 annual contributions allowed. Key Features of Trump Accounts Purpose: Long-term financial security/wealth growth for children. Government Seed: A one-time $1,000 deposit from the Treasury for children born Jan 1, 2025 – Dec 31, 2028. Funding: Parents, family, or employers can contribute up to $5,000 annually per child. Investments: Funds are invested in, for example, S&P 500 index ETFs. Withdrawals: Funds generally cannot be withdrawn before age 18, with some tax penalties for non-qualified expenses. Activation: Parents can make an election on IRS Form 4547 starting with the 2026 tax year. Eligibility and Management Eligibility: U.S. citizen children under 18 with a Social Security Number. Management: Parents or legal guardians act as custodians until the child turns 18. Post-18: At age 18, the account transitions to follow traditional IRA rules. Other Potential Considerations Some analysts argue these accounts, while designed to foster capitalism, add complexity to the tax code. The political branding might influence participation rates, despite potential financial advantages. Some institutions, such as the Michael and Susan Dell Foundation, have pledged additional funding for specific, eligible children.",
